 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "status": "todo", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+
+`status` is `"todo"` (the default), `"doing"` or `"done"`. Any other value answers `400` `{ "error": "status must be todo, doing or done" }`.
+
+**`done` is deprecated** and will be removed in the next release; use `status`. For now responses still carry `done`
+(`true` exactly when `status` is `done`), `PATCH` accepts `done: true` (status `done`) and `done: false` (status `todo`),
+and `GET /api/tasks?done=true|false` still works (`false` means `todo` or `doing`). When a body has both, `status` wins.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?status=todo\|doing\|done` keeps one status (400 for another value); deprecated: `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the not done ones | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "status": "doing" }` (`status` is optional) | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `status` (deprecated: `done`) | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
 ## Layout
